# Sanity — the CMS powering this site's content (projects, process, skills,
# about, contact, and job-application variants). Without these set, every
# page falls back to the local seed data in src/lib/data/ automatically —
# the site works either way, this just switches it to live content.
#
# Get these from sanity.io/manage after creating a project (see README.md
# "CMS setup" for the full walkthrough). Copy this file to .env.local and
# fill in the values — .env.local is gitignored, never commit real values.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_API_VERSION=2025-01-01

# --- Only needed once, when migrating content from the OLD portfolio's
# Sanity project. Not read by the app itself — see scripts/sanity/README.md.
# OLD_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
# OLD_SANITY_DATASET=production
# OLD_SANITY_TOKEN=
# NEW_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
# NEW_SANITY_DATASET=production
# NEW_SANITY_TOKEN=

# --- Privacy-safe visitor metrics (claps + the Overview "visitors from"
# panel). The app works without this — it just uses a fallback salt, which
# is fine for local dev but should be a real secret in production so the
# visitor hash isn't reproducible from a public value.
# VISITOR_HASH_SALT=

# --- Case-study comment box. Silently posts into a Google Form (a hidden
# iframe target, so there's no redirect to Google's response page) — get
# these from the form's prefilled-link URL (Send → get pre-filled link) and
# its entry.NNNNN field IDs. Comments are disabled (not broken) until the
# URL and comment entry ID are both set; the name field is optional.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COMMENT_FORM_URL=https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/FORM_ID/formResponse
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COMMENT_FORM_ENTRY_ID=entry.123456789
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COMMENT_FORM_NAME_ENTRY_ID=entry.987654321
